# Base egress allowlist for every devbox container.
#
# One entry per line, `#` starts a comment. An entry is either an IPv4 address or
# CIDR, which goes into the ipset as-is, or a hostname, which is resolved at
# container start (a name that fails to resolve is skipped with a warning — the
# firewall still applies).
#
# This file is the *floor*: what the image's own toolchain needs, plus Claude
# Code and the editor. Three other things add to it, and none of them belongs
# here:
#
#   scripts/<feature>/allowed-domains       merged while that feature is declared
#   projects/<profile>/allowed-domains      merged for the matching workspace
#   DEVBOX_ALLOW_DOMAINS=a.example b.example  one-off, at `devbox up` time
#
# Changing any of them takes effect on a container *restart* — the firewall is
# re-applied by postStartCommand — with no rebuild. Confirm what landed with
# `sudo ipset list allowed-domains`.
#
# Anthropic's network access requirements list what Claude Code itself needs:
# https://code.claude.com/docs/en/network-config#network-access-requirements

# Nothing for turbo's cache: it is a bind-mounted host directory, not a server,
# so it needs no egress at all. The CIDR that used to be here belonged to the
# remote cache in turbo-cache/docker-compose.yml — put it back together with
# everything else in that file's header if you ever re-wire it.

# --- GitHub -------------------------------------------------------------------
# The published IP ranges are fetched from api.github.com/meta at start; these
# names cover the Azure-hosted endpoints outside those blocks, and keep git
# usable when the fetch fails.
github.com
api.github.com
codeload.github.com
raw.githubusercontent.com
objects.githubusercontent.com

